==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Nagisa & Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Law of Cycles Nagisa''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bebe/Nagisa & Cat shares the same concept as the Ubers from the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS]] event. Their unevolved form has lower stats but a shorter cooldown compared to their Evolved form.

However, unlike the unevolved form of ULTRA SOULS ubers, Bebe has a cooldown of a typical Super Rare Unit. Bebe's weaken ability has rather low uptime, and thus they cannot consistently weaken [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies. This can be solved by stacking multiple of them, but it will be difficult to accomplish due to their long cooldown. Furthermore, stacking multiple Bebes isn't an easy task when facing Zombies since they can randomly hit or kill Bebe from their burrowing attack, not to mention that Bebe has rather low health.

Just like the Evolved from of ULTRA SOULS ubers, Nagisa & Cat now has better stats with significantly improved weaken uptime. With improved stats, range and weaken uptime, Nagisa & Cat now has the ability to perma-weaken Alien/Zombie enemies at a safe range with all of [[Cats of the Cosmos]]'s [[Antimatter Fruit|Antimatter]] and [[Enigma Fruit]] treasures. Thanks to her higher range, she can also outrange several dangerous Alien and Zombie enemies such as [[Cadaver Bear]], [[Ursamajor]] and [[Le'Solar]]. Unlike regular backline Ubers, Nagisa & Cat has a surprisingly high knockback count, which makes her last longer against Zombies as she can reposition multiple times even after Zombies' burrowing attacks.

Nagisa & Cat performs very well against Zombies due to the fact that most of them are melee. The only Zombies enemies she can't consistently weaken are [[Zamelle]], because of it having 550 range, as well as [[Daboo of the Dead]] and [[Death Angel Z-Onel]]. Against Aliens, her Immune to Warp may seem difficult to judge at first glance, but is actually very beneficial for Nagisa since she already has 6 knockbacks to reposition herself behind meatshields. It may be useful in stages such as [[Glass Slippers]] where [[Gardeneel Bros.]] are there to warp your cats into the [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]]'s attack range. Nagisa & Cat also has a relatively short cooldown and low cost for an Uber.

==='''True Form'''===
Her True Form adds a few minor changes. Firstly, she gets multi-hit, but due to the negligible damage its only purpose is to serve as an extension to her debuff duration.

She also gains two more abilities, barrier breaker and dodge, both making her significantly more usable. Her barrier breaker is always good to have, but especially on a debuff unit, as it allows her to weaken more Starred Aliens. Her dodge, while still being nice against Aliens, is even better for burrowing zombies. Because in her Evolved Form, despite her range, if a zombie burrows next to her she would lose a large chunk of her health. Now with her 2 second dodge, she has a chance to tank the zombie and maybe get a hit in while support helps kill it. All and all, a solid true form for a solid unit. The true form cost is very cheap too.

